`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- I checked the sibling `com.google.http-client:google-http-client` entry already in this repo's `metadata/` tree first, since it's published by the same GitHub org (googleapis) with a nearly identical build setup. That entry already preferred Maven Central's `-sources.jar`/`-tests.jar`/`-javadoc.jar` URLs over GitHub tag links — matching the task's explicit preference for Maven-hosted artifacts when available — so I mirrored that exact pattern rather than inventing a new convention.
- I verified each of the three Maven Central URLs with `curl -I` (HTTP 200) and listed the directory before trusting them, rather than constructing them from the version number and assuming they'd resolve — Maven Central doesn't always publish a `-tests.jar` for every artifact, so this check matters.
- `google-oauth-client` is a pure-Java artifact with no Android/JS/native-specific variant, so neither "language" nor "not-for-native-image" applies — unlike, say, a Kotlin or Android-only AAR artifact where those fields would be required.
